BUG-S2-01 / TC-S2-TST-06-A: User Cannot Access/View Products and Customers
Severity / Priority: High / P1
Environment: Sprint 2 Integration Build (Frontend UI + Backend RBAC Middleware)

Steps to Reproduce:
-Log in using a standard approved user account (status = 'Active', is_blocked = false).
-Attempt to navigate to the Customers and Products modules from the dashboard or sidebar.
-Observe access denial / missing module visibility even when the user should be granted read access.

Expected Behavior: Users granted Customer and Product view permissions can view the Customers and Products directories without error, while ungranted users receive a clear permission denial
Root Cause & Triage Notes: Directly coupled with BUG-S2-02—because the Superadmin could not persist rights assignments in User Management, standard user accounts remained without public.user_permission entries for Customer and Product modules.
Fix Verification (TC-S2-TST-06-A): After applying the User Management rights fix (BUG-S2-02) and assigning Customer/Product view rights, logged in as the standard user and confirmed both the Customers and Products lists load cleanly with zero regressions.

Status: PASS / Verified Fixed✅

BUG-S2-02 / TC-S2-TST-06-B: User Management Not Functioning Properly (Superadmin Could Not Give Rights to User)
Severity / Priority: Critical / P1
Environment: Sprint 2 Integration Build (User Management & Rights Dialog)

Steps to Reproduce:
-Log in as the Superadmin account (public.app_user joined to public.role).
-Open User Management, select an active user account, and open the Rights / Permissions assignment dialog.
-Toggle module/action rights (Customer, Product, Price History) and click Save.

Expected Behavior: Superadmin can open the Rights dialog for any user, grant or revoke individual rights, and persist those selections cleanly in public.user_permission.
Root Cause & Triage Notes: Superadmin role authorization / rights update endpoint failed to commit permission changes to public.user_permission.
Fix Verification (TC-S2-TST-06-B): Logged in as Superadmin, assigned granular Customer, Product, and Price rights to a test user, confirmed rows updated in public.user_permission, and verified the changes immediately took effect upon user login.

Status: PASS / Verified Fixed ✅

